---
description: Design handoff rules for the Space-Only Blocks feature (KIS Creativity Space)
alwaysApply: false
---

When implementing the Space-Only Blocks feature:

- The spec is handoff_cursor_space_only_blocks/README.md — source of truth for scope semantics, colors, and copy. Values are exact, not suggestions.
- designs/*.dc.html are HTML prototypes for behavior reference only. Never copy their markup, the DCLogic classes, or support.js into the codebase.
- Scope matrix: "all" blocks both consumers; "training" blocks only Book training; "space" blocks only the public Schedule. Missing scope = "all". Enforce server-side, not just in the UI.
- Space-only styling is the blue-grey family (#e6edf4 / #b9cede / #3b6285); training-only stays amber; full blocks stay grey.
- The creation-time overlap warning is suppressed ONLY for scope "training" — space-only blocks do affect space bookings.
- Scope changes via the per-row toggle remain immediate persisted updates with toast + Undo, never a confirm dialog.
